From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Changwoo Min <changwoo@igalia.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 15:56:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] scx_lavd: fix neighbor migration never firing on non-SMT
 machines

pick_idle_cpu() gates neighbor migration on !i_smt_empty, but on a machine
without SMT it set i_smt_empty to true unconditionally. So a waking task
could never be donated to a neighbor cpdom. Without SMT a core is a CPU, so
alias the SMT mask to the idle cpumask and derive i_smt_empty from it. The
fully-idle fast paths come alive too, harmlessly.

Measured with memtier_benchmark against memcached on a 2x96-core EPYC 9R45
without SMT, 24 LLC domains of 8 CPUs, 10 runs per point, --performance
with 3-10 ms slices. Throughput is unchanged within the run-to-run spread
(-1.8% to +0.7%). The tail improves where domains get crowded: pinned to
two LLCs at 75% of saturation, p99 drops from 7.34 to 6.86 ms and p99.9
from 13.45 to 10.97 ms; unpinned at 75%, p99 drops from 5.27 to 3.99 ms
with p99.9 flat. At 100% the tails are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Changwoo Min <changwoo@igalia.com>
---
 scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/idle.bpf.c | 18 +++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/idle.bpf.c b/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/idle.bpf.c
index 1ae10aa70..b2b367f42 100644
--- a/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/idle.bpf.c
+++ b/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/idle.bpf.c
@@ -865,7 +865,8 @@ s32 pick_idle_cpu(struct pick_ctx *ctx, bool extend_ovrflw, bool *is_idle)
 	/* NOTE: There is a sticky domain. */
 
 	/*
-	 * If there is no idle CPU, stay on the sticky CPU or domain.
+	 * If there is no idle CPU even partially,
+	 * stay on the sticky CPU or domain.
 	 */
 	idle_cpumask = scx_bpf_get_idle_cpumask();
 	if (!init_idle_i_mask(ctx, idle_cpumask))
@@ -881,13 +882,13 @@ s32 pick_idle_cpu(struct pick_ctx *ctx, bool extend_ovrflw, bool *is_idle)
 	/* NOTE: There is at least one idle CPU. */
 
 	/*
-	 * If SMT is enabled and the sticky CPU is fully idle, stay on it.
+	 * If the sticky CPU is fully idle, stay on it.
 	 */
-	if (is_smt_active) {
+	if (is_smt_active)
 		idle_smtmask = scx_bpf_get_idle_smtmask();
-		i_smt_empty = bpf_cpumask_empty(idle_smtmask);
-	} else
-		i_smt_empty = true;
+	else
+		idle_smtmask = idle_cpumask;
+	i_smt_empty = bpf_cpumask_empty(idle_smtmask);
 
 	if (!i_smt_empty && sticky_cpu >= 0 &&
 	    bpf_cpumask_test_cpu(sticky_cpu, idle_smtmask) &&
@@ -898,8 +899,7 @@ s32 pick_idle_cpu(struct pick_ctx *ctx, bool extend_ovrflw, bool *is_idle)
 	}
 
 	/*
-	 * If SMT is enabled and there is a fully idle CPU
-	 * in the sticky domain, stay on it.
+	 * If there is a fully idle CPU in the sticky domain, stay on it.
 	 */
 	if (!i_smt_empty) {
 		if (!init_idle_ato_masks(ctx, idle_smtmask))
@@ -1047,7 +1047,7 @@ unlock_out:
 	/*
 	 * Clean up.
 	 */
-	if (idle_smtmask)
+	if (is_smt_active && idle_smtmask)
 		scx_bpf_put_idle_cpumask(idle_smtmask);
 	if (idle_cpumask)
 		scx_bpf_put_idle_cpumask(idle_cpumask);
-- 
